  "result": "The gate's final verdict is **WITNESS_FAIL**, and the cause is the run's reading of the bus and taxicab aggregates, not the Lean. 12 of the 14 witnesses pass: forbid, permit, idle, blind and branch_3 to branch_10. The two planned branches can only come out unknown:\n\n- **branch_1** (a car stopped with a door open while a bus waits nearby) can never be violated. The reading puts no class at all in `DEF-NRS-484A-030::bus` or `DEF-NRS-484A-270::taxicab`, so no road user is ever decidedly a bus or a taxicab.\n- **branch_2** (a truck in a taxicab stand) can never be violated either. Every vehicle class, `ru.taxicab` included, is left unresolved for the taxicab aggregate, so no vehicle is ever decidedly not a taxicab. That leaves the taxicab-stand part of the applicability permanently unknown.\n- **Knock-on effect:** only a road user whose sole class is `taxicab` is decidedly a vehicle and decidedly not a bus. So the truck/trailer test and the \"interferes with a waiting bus or taxicab\" test can't be exercised by any decided witness.\n\n**What needs to change:** the reading should include `ru.bus`, `ru.transit_bus` and `ru.school_bus` in the bus aggregate and `ru.taxicab` in the taxicab aggregate. Otherwise the plan has to drop branch_1 and branch_2 as violated and stop using a bus for idle.\n\nSome witnesses differ from their narratives because of this, and the differences need your review:\n- **forbid, permit, blind:** the \"passenger car\" has class `taxicab` alone, the only class that works.\n- **blind:** it uses a bus stop rather than a taxicab stand, so that the hidden door state is what makes the result unknown.\n- **idle:** it puts the car in a passenger-loading zone instead of a bus in a bus stop.\n\nThe rule follows the record as written, with no narrowings declared. I added branch_3 to branch_10 to cover each way a halt is excused: each traffic-control device, the officer, and queueing behind another vehicle.\n\nGate runs: the first full run failed to build because of an extra parenthesis, which I fixed. The second gave the result above. Before those, a command I sent by mistake may have run the gate once against the harness's unfilled files and used a run from the budget. I stopped there because nothing in the two files can change these two results.\n\nEverything is in `task_result.md`, including the choices I made where the record left the wording open.",
